<title>AUSTRIA: ALPINE SKIING-SEIZINGER WINS OPENING GIANT SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-SEIZINGER WINS OPENING GIANT SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>SOELDEN, Austria 1996-10-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Katja Seizinger of Germany won the season-opening Alpine skiing World Cup women's giant slalom in a combined time of two minutes 11.81 seconds on Saturday, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Italian Deborah Compagnoni was second in 2:11.93 and Hilde Gerg of Germany was third in 2:13.84, also according to provisional results.</p>
</text>
